Sectoare de activitate: Angajare și recrutare de personal și Servicii IT și consultanță IT
Description 
 Akindra Talents is a Romania-based IT workforce company providing flexible IT staffing solutions and support to global customers. Based in the heart of Transylvania, we focus on connecting talented individuals with our clients across Europe. We build and manage remote operational support and development teams, while also supporting our freelance collaborators during their journey.
 Our client is a global trading, logistics, and distribution company headquartered in Belgium, with over 180 locations worldwide. Our client specializes in the distribution of chemicals across emerging markets worldwide, focusing on industries such as home care, nutrition, and mining. The company has its own local logistics assets and provides services including storage, value-added logistics, and just-in-time deliveries. With over 3000 employees the annual revenues exceed 2.5 billion USD, reflecting its significant presence in the chemical distribution sector.
 To strengthen the global IT team, our client is looking for a BI Data Engineer to design, develop, and maintain scalable data pipelines and models to support business intelligence and reporting needs across global operations. The role ensures high-quality, trusted data is available for analytics, decision-making, and performance management. The BI Data Engineer will translate business needs into technical specifications and solutions.
 Responsibilities 
Design and build ETL/ELT pipelines to extract data from diverse sources;
Develop and optimise data models for BI and analytics platforms (e.g., Power BI, Azure);
Implement and manage data quality rules and data validation logic;
Collaborate with business users to understand reporting requirements;
Maintain and enhance the enterprise data warehouse environment;
Ensure security, compliance, and access controls on BI data assets;
Monitor data loads and resolve data-related issues;
Document data pipelines, structures, and technical specifications;
Support self-service BI by enabling standardised and trusted data sets;
Continuously optimise queries and storage to improve performance;
Performing technical analysis & solution design for projects and requests assigned to the team.
 Requirements 
+5 years of relevant / proven experience in (backend) data engineering;
Mandatory strong and proven skills in 
SQL;
data warehousing;
data modelling.
Proven Experience and track record with 
Power BI;
Azure Data Factory;
Fabric;
DBT;
SQL;
Azure DEVOPS (boards & CI/CD pipelines).
Good knowledge of ETL/ELT best practices, and scripting (Python, DAX);
Good understanding of data governance, security, and lifecycle management;
Fluent in English;
Degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, or related field.
 Additional Information 
Permanent (CIM -direct with client)
Start: As soon as possible
Location: Bucharest, Hybrid
Language: English
